   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Liquid Metal\n\nA molten metal surface with flowing, chromatic highlights fills the frame, drawn in WebGL. Pick a shape to make it an emblem instead.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A premium, industrial or luxury scene wants a brushed, molten metal surface.\n- You want reflective, flowing highlights that read as material rather than color.\n- The palette is neutral or monochrome and you want the tint to lead subtly.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want a centered metallic emblem: set `shape` to circle, daisy, diamond or metaballs (it defaults to a full-bleed surface).\n- The brief calls for color: liquid-metal is tonal; use shader-mesh-gradient.\n- High contrast highlights would fight fine text: lower `contour` and `repetition`.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- color_back (color): Metal color, default \"#2a2a30\"\n- color_tint (color): Tint, default \"#8a8a95\"\n- distortion (number, 0-1): Distortion, default 0.1\n- repetition (number, 1-10): Repetition, default 1.5\n- contour (number, 0-1): Contour, default 0.4\n- softness (number, 0-1): Softness, default 0.05\n- shift_red (number, -1-1): Red shift, default 0.3\n- shift_blue (number, -1-1): Blue shift, default 0.3\n- angle (number, 0-360): Angle, default 70\n- shape (enum): Shape, default \"none\"\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
